 "result_text": "I changed `to_struct` in `stellar_sdk/scval.py` to sort the struct's field names before building the map. I haven't run it against the network or run any tests.\n\nThe likely cause is that Soroban requires `ScMap` keys to be in sorted order. `to_struct` kept the dict's insertion order. In your example that gives `source, asset, price, timestamp`, which isn't sorted, so the host rejects it with \"failed to convert ScVal to host value\". Your XDR shape was otherwise correct. With the fix, the same struct is encoded as `asset, price, source, timestamp`.\n\n`to_map` itself is unchanged. If you build a map by hand with `to_map` and unsorted keys, you'll hit the same error. I left it alone because the host orders keys by value, and getting that right for arbitrary key types is more involved than sorting symbol names.",
